Hello,

Download the MT_TA_ImportFunction.m (must) and the TA_DataAnalysis.m (optional) file into the directory containing the data files. You can call the import funtion MT_TA_ImportFunction.m by the following syntax in any script or in the command window
NameYouWant = MT_TA_ImportFunction();

The MT_TA_ImportFunction.m file helps you to import FSC or DSC data collected by MT Flash DSC or MT DSC 3+ in a matter of seconds.

This code imports all segments regardless of their nature, either as isothermal or dynamic heating/cooling, and stores them in separate bins in a MATLAB struct.

Your data must be in .txt format and must be exported from starE with the exact name given by it. Because the code reads that specific name and identifies how many segments are there in your experiment.

You can import as many data files as you want using this code. In other words, you can select multiple data files once prompted and all of them will be imported into the same struct.

Once imported, you will see the following,

    Col 1 (File)   === The filename of the datafile
    Col 2 (Mass)   === The mass of the sample. A numeric value will be displayed for DSC data (this is the sample mass you enter when setting up the experiment) and it will show zero for FSC as there is no mass value entered for FSC experiments initially.
    Col 3 (Data)   === All raw data before binning into either isothermal or dynamic
    Col 4 (Iso)    === All isothermal data
        Iso.Col 1 === Struct containing all information about the isothermal hold
          Iso.Col 1. Col 1 (Index)   === Segment Number
          Iso.Col 1. Col 2 (Name)    === Segment Name
          Iso.Col 1. Col 3 (Values)  === Data
          Iso.Col 1. Col 4 (Type)    === Bin type (isothermal)
          Iso.Col 1. Col 5 (IsoTemp) === Isothermal temperature
          Iso.Col 1. Col 6 (IsoHold) === Isothermal hold time

        Iso.Col 2 === Isothermal temperature
        Iso.Col 3 === Isothermal hold time

    Col 5 (Dynamic) === All dynamic data
        Dynamic.Col 1 (All)     === All dynamic data before binning to heating or cooling
        Dynamic.Col 2 (Heating) === All heating data
          Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1 === Heating data
            Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1. Col 1 === Index
            Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1. Col 2 === Time
            Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1. Col 3 === Sample temperature
            Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1. Col 4 === Reference temperature
            Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1. Col 5 === Heat flow rate in mW

          Dynamic.Col 2. Col 2 === Previous isothermal hold time before the heating segment
          Dynamic.Col 2. Col 3 === Heating rate in K/s

        Dynamic.Col 2 (Cooling) === All cooling data
          Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1 === Cooling data
            Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1. Col 1 === Index
            Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1. Col 2 === Time
            Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1. Col 3 === Sample temperature
            Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1. Col 4 === Reference temperature
            Dynamic.Col 2. Col 1. Col 5 === Heat flow rate in mW

          Dynamic.Col 2. Col 2 === Previous isothermal hold time before the cooling segment
          Dynamic.Col 2. Col 3 === Cooling rate in K/s


Enjoy!

